  "article": {
    "id": "re-foundations-8a-a-penguin-s-year",
    "title": "RE Foundations / 8A / A Penguin’s Year",
    "text_type": "informational",
    "audience": {
      "grade_band": "upper_elementary"
    },
    "language": "en"
  },
  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "Emperor penguins are the largest penguins on Earth."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "Each adult is over a meter tall, and can weigh up to 40 kilograms."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "For many months each year, emperors live near the sea in large groups."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "However, the weather gets colder in May, and ice covers large areas of ocean."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "Each group moves many kilometers from the water."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "There, each mother penguin lays just a single egg."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "Then all the hungry mothers walk back to the ocean to find food."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "The father penguins put their eggs on top of their feet."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "They cover the eggs with a special piece of skin called the brood pouch."
          },
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "up to Who will protect the eggs?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "Which month is the coldest in Antarctica?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "For two months, the father penguins protect the eggs and keep them warm."
          },
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "They do this through some of the coldest weather conditions on Earth."
          },
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "By July, it is winter in Antarctica."
          },
          {
            "id": "s15",
            "text": "Most other animals leave for warmer places, but the father penguins stay."
          },
          {
            "id": "s16",
            "text": "weather conditions When does the mother penguin return?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s17",
            "text": "Why must the penguin parents be careful?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "order": 4,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s18",
            "text": "By August, each mother penguin returns just in time to see her baby hatch 1."
          },
          {
            "id": "s19",
            "text": "The chick 2 is then moved to her brood pouch."
          },
          {
            "id": "s20",
            "text": "This can be difficult."
          },
          {
            "id": "s21",
            "text": "If the chick falls, it can freeze quickly."
          },
          {
            "id": "s22",
            "text": "The penguin parents must be very careful."
          },
          {
            "id": "s23",
            "text": "Once the chick has been moved, the father penguin can go back to the ocean to find food."
          },
          {
            "id": "s24",
            "text": "Which one will look for food for the chick?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "order": 5,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s25",
            "text": "Over the next few months, penguin parents take turns 3 going to the ocean for food."
          },
          {
            "id": "s26",
            "text": "They each make the trip several times, bringing back food for the chick."
          },
          {
            "id": "s27",
            "text": "The chick is always hungry and grows rapidly."
          },
          {
            "id": "s28",
            "text": "When can the chick live on its own?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "order": 6,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s29",
            "text": "By December, winter is ending."
          },
          {
            "id": "s30",
            "text": "The chick can now live on its own."
          },
          {
            "id": "s31",
            "text": "Soon it enters the water for the first time."
          },
          {
            "id": "s32",
            "text": "It will swim and eat until next April, and then return."
          },
          {
            "id": "s33",
            "text": "After a few more years, it, too, will start its own family."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
